put.description:
Store one of the caller's organizations as active; the token in hand still names the previous one.

Refresh the token (refresh-token grant at the identity provider's token endpoint; `databay org switch`
does it) and the new token names this one. Refusals:

- 403 `org_not_member`: the caller does not belong to that organization;
- 403 `org_disabled`: the organization is disabled, so no token could name it;
- 403 `api_key_not_allowed`: the caller is an org API key, which belongs to one organization;
- 503 `auth_unavailable`: the identity provider could not be read or written; retry later;
- 500 `active_org_not_stored`: the identity provider dropped the choice; nothing was switched.

post.description:
Place a card of the project on its Overview dashboard and answer that dashboard.

The project's first pin creates an ordinary dashboard named "Overview" and makes it the Overview;
a card already there is 409 ``card_already_on_board``.
